[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The reports say
three. They were merged on their subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and their subjects are the same whatever went wrong, so one fix will not close them all.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first row. The other two need their own fixes, so each
now has its own ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the day and month swap. A day-first tenant's date goes through the shared parser
  and comes out month first: 7 April becomes 4 July. It reaches us through the app, email and
  forms that print the tenant's own order.
- **`hint`**: also a swap, but the parser is not to blame. booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
  its date field, people type what it tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way.
  Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants. Fixing the parser does not touch it; fixing the
  hint does.
- **`move`**: not a swap. The date is one day off ("Tuesday 12 May, calendar says Monday 11 May"),
  or two people in different cities see different days for one meeting. The desk already read
  these apart ([desk notes](/kb/incidents/4471)); they were filed under `parser` only because of
  their tenant. Day and month order cannot move a date by one day, so this is a third bug,
  most likely in how the time zone is applied.

## For the desk

- Count a merged ticket by cause, not by subject. The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's
  browser and is wrong in both directions here.
- Keep #4471 open until each of the three tickets is closed.

